37\r\n+ ... or ($i=$range[0]; $i -le [Math]::Min($range[1],$lines.Length); $i++)  ...\r\n+                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n    + CategoryInfo          : OperationStopped: (:) [], ArgumentException\r\n    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : System.ArgumentException\r\n \r\nFILE docs/development/testing.md\r\n 213: ## Submitter access request coverage\r\n 214: \r\n 215: The submitter-access API and repository suites cover:\r\n 216: \r\n 217: - anonymous requests being rejected before request processing;\r\n 218: - an authenticated application account creating a `pending` request;\r\n 219: - the authenticated account being passed to the request service;\r\n 220: - duplicate `pending` requests returning a conflict;\r\n 221: - accounts with the legacy `approved` request state returning a conflict;\r\n 222: - eligible state changes being implemented as a conditional database update; and\r\n 223: - unsupported persisted approval states failing closed.\r\n 224: \r\n 225: The PostgreSQL integration suite additionally verifies that `not_requested` and previously `rejected` accounts persist as `pending`, a second active request is rejected, and an already-approved account is not modified.\r\n 226: \r\n 227: Run the focused checks with:\r\n 228: \r\n 229: ```text\r\n 230: npm run build --workspace=@sport-analytics/contracts\r\n 231: npm run typecheck --workspace=@sport-analytics/backend\r\n 232: npm exec --workspace=@sport-analytics/backend -- vitest run tests/api/submitter-access-request.test.ts\r\n 233: npm exec --workspace=@sport-analytics/backend -- vitest run tests/unit/submitter-access.repository.test.ts\r\n 234: npm run test:database --workspace=@sport-analytics/backend\r\n 235: ```\r\n 236: \r\n 237: An explicitly configured database integration run requires `NODE_ENV=test` and a dedicated\r\n 238: `DATABASE_URL_TEST`. It must not run against the shared development or production database. With no\r\n 239: configured URL, the embedded disposable workflow described above is used. The supported scripts set\r\n 240: `NODE_ENV=test` automatically, and destructive operations validate that the target is isolated from\r\n 241: the development database.\r\n 242: \r\n 243: ## Current-user submitter status coverage\r\n 244: \r\n 245: The current-user profile contract and authentication suites verify that `/api/v1/auth/me`\r\n 246: exposes persisted submitter-access state for authenticated application accounts.\r\n 247: \r\n 248: Coverage includes:\r\n 249: \r\n 250: - `not_requested`, `pending`, `approved`, and `rejected` approval states;\r\n 251: - shared runtime validation of the complete current-user response through\r\n 252:   `@sport-analytics/contracts`;\r\n 253: - API responses reflecting the synchronized account approval state;\r\n 254: - account re-authentication updating identity metadata without overwriting persisted role or\r\n 255:   submitter approval state;\r\n 256: - current-user resolution during the ordered role and account-deletion migration rollout, including\r\n 257:   legacy approved submitters and administrators;\r\n 258: - frontend rejection of malformed current-user responses rather than inferring access from\r\n 259:   incomplete data;\r\n 260: - explicit unauthenticated and server-error status states; and\r\n 261: - a successful retry after a transient status-loading failure.\r\n 262: \r\n 263: Run the focused checks with:\r\n 264: \r\n 265: ```text\r\n 266: npm run build --workspace=@sport-analytics/contracts\r\n 267: npm run test --workspace=@sport-analytics/contracts\r\n 268: npm run test:unit --workspace=@sport-analytics/backend\r\n 269: npm run test:api --workspace=@sport-analytics/backend\r\n 270: npm run test --workspace=@sport-analytics/frontend\r\n 271: ```\r\n 272: \r\n 273: ## Submitter access frontend coverage\r\n 274: \r\n 275: The Account-page suite verifies the complete user-facing request workflow:\r\n 276: \r\n 277: - signed-out users do not load application account data;\r\n 278: - eligible users can request access and see an in-progress state;\r\n 279: - successful requests reload the persisted `pending` profile;\r\n 280: - a remount restores `pending` without offering another request;\r\n 281: - stale eligible views refresh after the backend reports an active-request conflict;\r\n 282: - `submitter` and `admin` roles receive submission access without a request action;\r\n 283: - a legacy `approved` request state on a viewer does not grant submission access;\r\n 284: - rejected users receive a clear state and may request another review, while revoked viewers retain\r\n 285:   the historical approved decision without submission access; and\r\n 286: - malformed profiles and backend request failures produce safe, actionable feedback.\r\n 287: \r\n 288: The request-response contract suite additionally verifies that only a persisted `pending` result is\r\n 289: accepted from the submitter-access endpoint. The browser suite verifies keyboard activation,\r\n 290: pending state after reload, narrow-screen overflow, and serious or critical Axe findings.\r\n 291: \r\n 292: The administrator-management suites verify that `not_requested` and `rejected` viewers have no\r\n 293: approval or competition-scope controls, pending viewers can be approved or rejected, and approved\r\n 294: submitters can still be re-scoped or revoked. Rejection coverage includes in-progress, success,\r\n 295: authentication, authorisation, conflict, and validation feedback. The administrator browser\r\n 296: scenario activates rejection from the keyboard at desktop and mobile widths, checks the immediate\r\n 297: persisted-state update and horizontal overflow, and scans the result for serious or critical Axe\r\n 298: findings. Backend policy, API, and PostgreSQL integration tests\r\n 299: also verify that a direct approval attempt without a pending request returns a conflict and cannot\r\n 300: bypass the state transition.\r\n 301: \r\n 302: Run the focused checks with:\r\n 303: \r\n 304: ```text\r\n 305: npm run build --workspace=@sport-analytics/contracts\r\n 306: npm run test --workspace=@sport-analytics/contracts\r\n 307: npm run test --workspace=@sport-analytics/frontend\r\n 308: npm run test:e2e -- tests/e2e/submitter-access.spec.ts --workers=1\r\n 309: ```\r\n 310: \r\n 311: ## Direct submission coverage\r\n 312: \r\n 313: The contract and API suites cover the versioned delivery schema, anonymous users and viewers,\r\n 314: in-scope and out-of-scope submitters, permitted admin submission, detailed invalid-event responses,\r\n 315: the JSON payload limit, and\r\n 316: the per-account rate limit. PostgreSQL integration tests verify stored provenance, submitted order,\r\n 317: duplicate event-ID rejection, and full rollback when a later event conflicts after an earlier insert.\r\n 318: \r\n 319: Run the focused checks with:\r\n 320: \r\n 321: ```text\r\n 322: npm run test --workspace=@sport-analytics/contracts\r\n 323: npm run test:api --workspace=@sport-analytics/backend\r\n 324: npm run db:test:reset --workspace=@sport-analytics/backend\r\n 325: npm run test:database --workspace=@sport-analytics/backend\r\n 326: npm run openapi:lint\r\n 327: ```\r\n 328: \r\n 329: The issue #51 verification record is in\r\n 330: `evidence/validation/issue-51-direct-event-submission.md` at the repository root.\r\n 331: \r\n 332: ## Submitter interface coverage\r\n 333: \r\n 334: The frontend suite covers anonymous redirection, role-denied viewers, submitter/admin role gates,\r\n 335: competition-scoped fixture selection, valid submissions, event- and field-specific validation\r\n 336: results, invalid JSON, and backend failures. Browser tests additionally verify keyboard order,\r\n 337: focus movement to results,\r\n 338: error association, narrow-screen overflow, and serious or critical Axe findings.\r\n 339: \r\n 340: Run the focused checks with:\r\n 341: \r\n 342: ```text\r\n 343: npm run build --workspace=@sport-analytics/contracts\r\n 344: npm run test --workspace=@sport-analytics/frontend\r\n 345: npm run test:e2e -- tests/e2e/submissions.spec.ts --workers=1\r\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"EXIT 0"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a03f37-16af-76c1-b09e-c41792572355","create_time":1787769158.718425}}}
